                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mark+Van+Raamsdonk"} Mark Van Raamsdonk
                = succeed "," do
                  %em M2-branes on M-folds
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0804.1256"} arXiv:0804.1256
          %p Review:
          %ul
            %li#BaggerLambert12
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jonathan+Bagger"}> Jonathan Bagger
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Neil+Lambert"} Neil Lambert
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sunil+Mukhi"} Sunil Mukhi
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Constantinos+Papageorgakis"} Constantinos Papageorgakis
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Multiple Membranes in M-theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1203.3546"} arXiv:1203.3546
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.physrep.2013.01.006"} doi:10.1016/j.physrep.2013.01.006
            %li#Lambert12
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Neil+Lambert"}> Neil Lambert
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em M-Theory and Maximally Supersymmetric Gauge Theories
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1203.4244"} arXiv:1203.4244
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1146/annurev-nucl-102010-130248"} doi:10.1146/annurev-nucl-102010-130248
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Neil+Lambert"}> Neil Lambert
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Lessons from M2’s and Hopes for M5’s
                %em
                  Proceedings of the
                  = succeed ":" do
                    %a{:href => "http://www.maths.dur.ac.uk/lms/"} LMS-EPSRC Durham Symposium
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Structures+in+M-Theory+2018"} Higher Structures in M-Theory 2018
                Fortschritte der Physik, 2019 (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1903.02825"}> arXiv:1903.02825
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.maths.dur.ac.uk/lms/109/talks/1877lambert.pdf"} slides pdf
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.maths.dur.ac.uk/lms/109/movies/1877lamb.mp4"} video recording
          %p
            Discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary+conditions"} boundary conditions
            leading to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/brane+intersection"} brane intersection
            with
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-wave"} M-wave
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-brane"} M5-brane
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MO9-brane"} MO9-brane
            is in
          %ul
            %li#ChuSmith09
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chong-Sun+Chu"}> Chong-Sun Chu
                , Douglas J. Smith,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Multiple Self-Dual Strings on M5-Branes
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0909.2333"} arXiv:0909.2333
            %li#BPST09
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Berman"}> David Berman
                , Malcolm J. Perry,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ergin+Sezgin"} Ergin Sezgin
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Boundary Conditions for Interacting Membranes
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0912.3504"} arXiv:0912.3504
          %p
            Discussion in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Horava-Witten+theory"} Horava-Witten theory
            reducing M2-branes to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+strings"} heterotic strings
            is in
          %ul
            %li#Lambert15
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Neil+Lambert"}> Neil Lambert
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Heterotic M2-branes
              %p
                Volume 749, 7 October 2015, Pages 363-367 (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1507.07931"}> arXiv:1507.07931
                )
          %p
            The interpretation of at least most of the “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M2-brane+3-algebra"}> M2-brane 3-algebra
            ” appearing in the membrane literature in terms of plain
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+Lie+algebras"} metric Lie algebras
            is due to
          %ul
            %li#MFMR
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+de+Medeiros"}> Paul de Medeiros
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jos%C3%A9+Figueroa-O%27Farrill"} José Figueroa-O'Farrill
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Elena+M%C3%A9ndez-Escobar"} Elena Méndez-Escobar
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Patricia+Ritter"} Patricia Ritter
              = succeed "," do
                %em On the Lie-algebraic origin of metric 3-algebras
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0809.1086"} arXiv:0809.1086
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jos%C3%A9+Figueroa-O%27Farrill"}> José Figueroa-O'Farrill
              ,
              %em Triple systems and Lie superalgebras
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %em M2-branes, ADE and Lie superalgebras
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://www.maths.ed.ac.uk/~jmf/CV/Seminars/Hongo.pdf"} pdf
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/FigueroaOFarrillM2Branes02.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p
            The suggestion that BGL “3-algebras” are to be interpreted in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-plectic+geometry"} 2-plectic geometry
            appears in
          %ul
            %li#SaemannSzabo
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christian+Saemann"}> Christian Saemann
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Richard+Szabo"} Richard Szabo
              %em Quantization of 2-Plectic Manifolds
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1106.1890"}> arXiv:1106.1890
              )
